From 8ce8e91bd9a90388daa7beccf78fdeabea54ed62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:39:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): propose recovery for pins absent from fresh
 registry [daveey]

Revoked machines disappear from the active-list registry, so requiring an
entry prevented their creator-owned cards from reaching Board adjudication.
Propose stale_pin for a single absent pin only after fresh valid membership
and the existing current portability/never-ran checks. The Board remains the
only assignment authority and distinguishes revoked from unknown names.

Validate raw registry shape before marking a fetch successful: missing or
malformed membership must not normalize to a fresh empty set. Keep cached
last-good offline discovery, but deny recovery after failed refresh. Reuse
the revision/cooldown refusal cache for pin_not_stale to bound unknown-name
proposals. Preserve owner move, CAS/source, labels, and active/held handling.

Proof: new regressions fail on base (11 failures); initial focused GREEN
47 passed. Added malformed-after-last-good and absent owner-move controls.
Whole-tree scripts/check passes all 20 checks. Direct consumer suite is
recorded on implementation card t_9d4bd881aa780900. Controlled deployed Board
fixture proof remains with parent t_334f72cc1c030696 after deployment.
